WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
Fourteen minutes past
three in the morning.

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:05.470
In the dark, a window gives way.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.320
Hard cut.

4
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.400
Sunlight.

5
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:11.590
Toast on the kitchen table,
and a radio chattering away.

6
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.510
Why would a writer tell it in this order,

7
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.200
and not simply start with breakfast?

8
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.040
In this mission, you'll
map the story twice:

9
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.810
in the order things happen,
and in the order they're told.

10
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:26.630
You'll track how the focus
shifts: zooming in on a detail,

11
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.640
out to a wider view, or back in time.

12
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.430
Is it just to grab your attention?

13
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.610
Or to confuse you on purpose?

14
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.050
You'll test both against the story.

15
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.280
Your mission: explain why the
story is told in this order.
